#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:5 1f3ccdfbe5d84b479ca65cd279319ea2
msgid "Archived: Troubleshooting"
msgstr "已归档：故障排除"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:9 3e01928d04b945f0bd850013b4adfdee
msgid ""
"This page has not been reviewed by the wiki approver team. It appears to "
"contain a lot of out of date and unverified material - June 2015."
msgstr "此页面尚未经过 wiki 审核团队审查。它似乎包含大量过时和未经验证的内容——2015年6月。"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:14 536a51116bf34ac8b340eaeea0316614
msgid "I can't get the motors to run and/or can't arm the ESCs"
msgstr "我无法让电机运转和/或无法解锁 ESC"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:16 0c37d22c8973460794aeeadf370e61f0
msgid "This can be due to a number of mistakes:"
msgstr "这可能是由于以下几种错误导致的："

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:18 b151cb2f0d5b4adc82da8b8a419188a3
msgid ""
"Have you completed the mandatory hardware configuration steps described "
":ref:`here <configuring-hardware>`?"
msgstr "您是否完成了 :ref:`此处 <configuring-hardware>` 描述的强制硬件配置步骤？"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:21 bca96b9347e14af988694e2f896e16e3
msgid ""
"Are you in Acro, Stabilize or Simple mode? As a safety measure, the motors "
"won't arm in other modes."
msgstr "您是否处于 Acro、Stabilize 或 Simple 模式？作为安全措施，电机在其他模式下不会解锁。"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:23 00c46a2c1a2c4f65816257c7d012e624
msgid ""
"Are you using the APM 2.5 Power Module to power the APM board, as "
"recommended? If not, and you're using one of your ESCs via the PDB to power "
"the board, make sure the JP1 jumper is on."
msgstr ""
"您是否按照建议使用 APM 2.5 电源模块为 APM 板供电？如果没有，而是使用 ESC 通过配电板为板供电，请确保 JP1 跳线已安装。"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:26 fb4b5512dd684989aec29691e6faa15e
msgid ""
"Are you sure you're arming them right? When the motors are armed, the arm "
"LED (green on APM1, yellow on APM 2) on the IMU will turn solid after the "
"IMU calibration flashing (about 5 seconds). Review the \\ :ref:`arming guide"
" <arming_the_motors>` to make sure you're doing it right."
msgstr ""
"您确定解锁方式正确吗？当电机解锁后，IMU 上的解锁指示灯（APM1 上为绿色，APM 2 上为黄色）在 IMU 校准闪烁（约 5 "
"秒）后会变为常亮。请查看 \\ :ref:`解锁指南 <arming_the_motors>` 确认操作正确。"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:31 03d7ffacd8f848869d3dcde8f52dda6f
msgid ""
"Are your Yaw or Throttle channels reversed on your transmitter? Try moving "
"the Yaw stick to the far left, instead of the right. If that works (green "
"LED tuns solid after the IMU calibration, your Yaw is reversed. If not, try "
"the same with the Throttle channel: push it to max and try full right yaw "
"from there. If that works, your Throttle channel is reversed."
msgstr ""
"您的遥控器上的偏航或油门通道是否反向？尝试将偏航摇杆向左移至最远处，而不是向右。如果这样可以工作（IMU 校准后绿色 LED "
"常亮），则您的偏航已反向。如果不行，对油门通道进行同样的尝试：将其推至最大并从那里向右全偏航。如果可以，则您的油门通道已反向。"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:37 63cdf1bca7474f2a89fa04fe971537fa
msgid ""
"Is your RC gear in Mode 2? If not, you'll need to move the right stick (yaw)"
" to the right and the left stick (throttle) to the top. (Or just switch back"
" to Mode 2)"
msgstr ""
"您的 RC 设备是否处于 Mode 2 模式？如果不是，您需要将右摇杆（偏航）向右移动，将左摇杆（油门）推至顶部。（或者直接切换回 Mode 2）"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:40
#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:430 1516db2fd81c4341875931e429580280
#: 6411702857ba4038875061d05219fa42
msgid ""
"Some ESCs are thrown off by some startup signals in Copter 2.x. Try plugging"
" in a USB cable first, to boot the board, and then plug in your LiPo after "
"it's already up, or just ensure that the four-wire cable from your APM board"
" to your power distribution board is disconnected during regular startup. "
"See details `here <https://diydrones.com/profiles/blogs/apm2-esc-startup-"
"problem-and-workaround>`__."
msgstr ""
"某些 ESC 会被 Copter 2.x 中的某些启动信号干扰。尝试先插入 USB 线缆引导板，然后在板已启动后再插入 "
"LiPo，或者确保在常规启动时断开从 APM 板到配电板的四线线缆连接。详情见 `此处 "
"<https://diydrones.com/profiles/blogs/apm2-esc-startup-problem-and-"
"workaround>`__。"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:46 fb46b7f71dc048138c7f0ae7c8cb27aa
msgid ""
"It's possible you've changed your throttle trim settings since you did your "
"initial radio calibration. Trim the throttle down a few notches and try "
"arming again."
msgstr "您可能自初始遥控器校准以来更改了油门微调设置。将油门向下微调几格并再次尝试解锁。"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:49 60977e92d3974f55944b9bedd39c73ed
msgid ""
"Some ESCs have a minimum low threshold before they will arm. If you need to,"
" trim down your radio throttle and redo radio calibration."
msgstr "某些 ESC 有最低阈值，低于该阈值不会解锁。如果需要，向下微调遥控器油门并重新进行遥控器校准。"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:51 d0c3f5f197294ba08897e3e107d9de1c
msgid ""
"Redo your radio calibration in the Mission Planner. Make sure that the "
"throttle channel (Ch 3) is being read properly and the values are around "
"1100 (low) and 1900 (high), more or less. Remember that your LiPo must be "
"plugged in to power the RC gear."
msgstr ""
"在 Mission Planner 中重新进行遥控器校准。确保油门通道（Ch 3）读取正确，数值大约在 1100（低）和 "
"1900（高）左右。请记住，必须插入 LiPo 电池为 RC 设备供电。"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:55 6fffe1c138c8487c8ae15ac78194a1f6
msgid ""
"If you've checked the previous things, it may be that you need to "
"recalibrate your ESCs. Do it the manual way (:ref:`here <esc-calibration>` "
"to be sure)."
msgstr "如果您已检查了上述事项，可能需要重新校准您的 ESC。请按手动方式进行（:ref:`此处 <esc-calibration>` 以确保）。"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:60 8d2f76558192493db1bf5dd238641c85
msgid "My APM 2 is locking up"
msgstr "我的 APM 2 锁死了"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:62 886b46f05f164636a70be9356ff75c9a
msgid ""
"The cause is probably that the dataflash card not initializing correctly. To"
" verify this is the problem, take it out and try to power your apm 2 again."
msgstr "原因可能是 dataflash 卡未正确初始化。要验证是否是此问题，请将其取出并再次尝试为 apm 2 供电。"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:66 34cae230550042ea991baa95fcf59cff
msgid ""
"If this is the case, there is an easy fix. Put the dataflash back in, and "
"power the board up while looking at the terminal screen. It will reformat "
"the card (this will take A WHILE). Leave it plugged in for 2 min. After that"
" you should see a \"ready to fly\" message. You only have to do this once."
msgstr ""
"如果是这种情况，有一个简单的解决方法。将 dataflash "
"卡重新插入，然后在查看终端屏幕的同时为板供电。它将重新格式化卡（这需要一段时间）。让它保持插入状态 2 分钟。之后您应该会看到\"ready to "
"fly\"消息。您只需执行一次此操作。"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:73 4ce43e8f96b740e78ad012e29de4bc6f
msgid "Copter tilts/flips over or wobbles crazily when I try to take off."
msgstr "Copter 在我尝试起飞时会倾斜/翻转，或者疯狂晃动。"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:75 01532df905b44910a1addf6471ac51da
msgid ""
"This almost always means that you've configured it or set it up wrong. Check"
" the following:"
msgstr "这几乎总是意味着您配置或设置有误。请检查以下内容："

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:78 9bfcf75e25b74df3bdd391407435ab59
msgid ""
"Is the APM board facing forward and in the direction of forward motion "
"(towards the forward arm in + mode and between the arms in x mode)?"
msgstr "APM 板是否朝向前方，并指向前进方向（+ 模式下朝向前臂，x 模式下在臂之间）？"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:81 7765b761c76a4c3cace7959662792e65
msgid "Have you set your quad orientation right in the setup process: + or x?"
msgstr "在设置过程中您是否正确设置了四轴方向：+ 还是 x？"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:83 3dbeab8ea8fb4744aebda3b9be1f4476
msgid ""
"Check that all the motors are hooked up right, turning the right way and the"
" pusher/puller props are on the right motors and oriented the right way."
msgstr "检查所有电机是否连接正确，旋转方向是否正确，以及推进/拉进型螺旋桨是否安装在正确的电机上并以正确方向安装。"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:86 67c83437817c4cf6b062460da747135f
msgid ""
"Check the signal wires on the power distribution board to make sure they are"
" oriented correctly. If you've reversed two, it will cause Copter to flip. "
"This should be noticeable by doing the hand test as well. (It should have "
"also shown up in the Motors test above)"
msgstr ""
"检查配电板上的信号线，确保它们方向正确。如果您颠倒了两根线，会导致 Copter "
"翻转。通过手持测试也应该注意到这一点。（在上方的电机测试中也应该显示出来）"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:90 058fae8b3b274eb7b87e08c207179c4b
msgid ""
"Check that your props can't turn on their motor shafts, as if they weren't "
"tightened down enough. If one can, despite its prop being tightened, that "
"may mean that its motor shaft has been pushed down into the motor too far "
"for the prop mount to get a grip. Take off the prop and and use a small "
"allen wrench to loosen the little set screw that holds the shaft onto the "
"motor. Then with pliers pull the shaft out until it's the same height as "
"those of the other motors. Then tighten the set screw, and put the prop back"
" and tighten it up again."
msgstr ""
"检查螺旋桨是否无法在电机轴上转动，就好像它们没有拧紧。如果某个螺旋桨在拧紧后仍然可以转动，这可能意味着电机轴被推入电机内部太深，螺旋桨固定座无法夹紧。取下螺旋桨，用小内六角扳手松开固定轴到电机的小顶丝。然后用钳子将轴拉出，直到与其他电机的轴高度相同。然后拧紧顶丝，重新安装螺旋桨并拧紧。"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:98 b649c0196fec47d4acc8c86684e01c9c
msgid ""
"Was the quad stable and flat for the whole calibration routine at startup? "
"Was it stable and flat during the setup process? (If need be, do it again)"
msgstr "在整个启动校准过程中，四轴是否稳定且平放？在设置过程中它是否稳定且平放？（如有必要，请重新进行）"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:101 cade78c95e0945dcb82c91c6bfa40ae7
msgid ""
"Did you calibrate your ESCs? They should all start together when you advance"
" the throttle. If need be, do it again manually, as described :ref:`here "
"<esc-calibration>`."
msgstr ""
"您是否校准了您的 ESC？当您推进油门时，所有 ESC 应同时启动。如有必要，请按照 :ref:`此处 <esc-calibration>` "
"的说明手动重新进行。"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:104 2810cad1b51645dab57b9819d22d5a09
msgid ""
"Did you setup and test your radio? Run test/radio to see. Pitch, Roll, "
"Throttle and Yaw should all be 0 or near zero (60 or less). Move the pitch "
"and roll stick to the lower right, you should see approximately 4500, 4500 "
"in Channels 1 and 2."
msgstr ""
"您是否设置并测试了遥控器？运行 test/radio 查看。俯仰、横滚、油门和偏航的值应该都为 0 或接近于零（60 "
"或以下）。将俯仰和横滚摇杆移至右下方，您应该看到通道 1 和 2 大约为 4500、4500。"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:108 c3e0328e0e9f484ead67fe38f05877cf
msgid ""
"Have you checked all your sensors in the Mission Planner to make sure the "
"hardware is working right?"
msgstr "您是否在 Mission Planner 中检查了所有传感器，确认硬件工作正常？"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:112 0fd53382e86b43dfbcd9994d43229505
msgid ""
"My overpowered copter rockets into the air can't be brought down unless I "
"cut the throttle"
msgstr "我的过度动力 Copter 飞速升空，除非关闭油门否则无法降落"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:114 1010d314e8594f39918d914880e917c3
msgid ""
"Very over powered multicopters can require so little throttle to hover that "
"even the minimum throttle (13%) is enough for them climb. In addition, the "
"default Rate roll/pitch gains, which are meant for weaker copter, are too "
"high for a powerful copter and can lead to roll/pitch instability. The "
"Copter firmware may try to compensate for this roll/pitch instability by "
"increasing the overall throttle which can lead to the copter climbing "
"further (Note: in this particular case Copter increasing the overall "
"throttle is counter-productive but in a properly tuned quad it helps in "
"cases where there is a motor failure)."
msgstr ""
"功率过大的多旋翼飞机可能仅需非常少的油门就能悬停，甚至最低油门（13%）就足以让它们爬升。此外，默认的横滚/俯仰速率增益是为较弱的 Copter "
"设计的，对于功率强劲的 Copter 来说太高，可能导致横滚/俯仰不稳定。Copter "
"固件可能会尝试通过增加整体油门来补偿这种横滚/俯仰不稳定，这可能导致 Copter 进一步爬升（注意：在这种特殊情况下，Copter "
"增加整体油门是适得其反的，但在调参良好的四轴上，这在电机故障时有帮助）。"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:124 48844d04c641457299e85b1f092358cb
msgid "The possible solutions are:"
msgstr "可能的解决方案是："

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:126 d4edd7b68c32400eb6c37110d8ae3672
msgid ""
"add extra weight to your frame to bring the hover throttle closer to mid "
"stick"
msgstr "在机架上增加额外重量，使悬停油门更接近中间位置"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:128 5f0f966bbe2046dd8eb07bc13c521918
msgid ""
"reduce the THR_MIN parameter (default is 130 or 13%) to the lowest value "
"that will still keep all motors spinning reliably"
msgstr "将 THR_MIN 参数（默认为 130 或 13%）降低到仍能保持所有电机可靠旋转的最低值"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:130 f5a77df34ca7483fa4edced7c79f55c8
msgid ""
"set the rate roll/pitch gains low (perhaps 1/2 the default) during the first"
" flight and increase them from there. Consider using the CH6 tuning feature "
"to allow you to tune your roll/pitch gains for the first few flights."
msgstr ""
"在首次飞行时将横滚/俯仰速率增益设低（约为默认值的 1/2），然后从那里开始增加。考虑使用 CH6 调参功能，让您在前几次飞行中调整横滚/俯仰增益。"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:138 d3f2090bc0c9475eb8284611cf0b13bb
msgid ""
"My copter motors spin but the copter won't take off (or motors may not spin "
"at all)"
msgstr "我的 Copter 电机旋转但 Copter 无法起飞（或电机可能完全不旋转）"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:140 d03cf93d90134203898c47907f09a838
msgid ""
"While there are a few different reasons for copters to be perceived as "
"underpowered, this condition applies to motors that simply aren't spinning "
"fast enough (if at all!) to generate the lift needed, even though you know "
"they can spin faster.  Some instances discovered recently showed someone had"
" accidentally imported the wrong parameter file into their copter from the "
"3D Robotics Aero, and when they then loaded the correct parameter file, the "
"THR_MAX parameter was left unchanged."
msgstr ""
"虽然有几种不同原因可能使 Copter "
"表现为动力不足，但这种情况适用于电机根本无法高速旋转（甚至完全不转！）以产生足够升力的情况，尽管您知道它们可以转得更快。最近发现的一些情况显示，有人不小心将"
" 3D Robotics Aero 的错误参数文件导入到他们的 Copter 中，当他们随后加载正确的参数文件时，THR_MAX 参数保持不变。"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:149
#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:165 c29d6a5acb35442b98c61806c54d67da
#: ecbbee7a2f304649a043bf88a662bae1
msgid "Check the following:"
msgstr "请检查以下内容："

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:151 cc98b1eb9f6d4d35834cfb28a988029a
msgid "Connect to the copter via your GCS"
msgstr "通过您的 GCS 连接到 Copter"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:152 33efa3bdae4244a08094c3d2cc31d248
msgid "Go to Full Parameter List"
msgstr "进入完整参数列表"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:153 4dc8a0f5336d40b6a065cc670bf7bdf8
msgid ""
"Examine the THR_MAX parameter and make sure the value is between 800 and "
"1000.  The default is 1000."
msgstr "检查 THR_MAX 参数，确保其值在 800 到 1000 之间。默认值为 1000。"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:156 0ed8279237084dd8b5c00136747cf01f
msgid "FYI: The 3D Robotics Aero preset param file sets this to 80."
msgstr "注：3D Robotics Aero 预设参数文件将此值设置为 80。"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:158 dfabca06d4194c1f9d75d4bd91c61379
msgid ""
"If the THR_MAX parameter is less than 800 and you don't recall making this "
"change, set the parameter to 1000 and Write Params out to the copter"
msgstr "如果 THR_MAX 参数小于 800 且您不记得做过此更改，请将参数设置为 1000 并将参数写入 Copter"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:163 197e3cd0d032405f8b60e26a0018ac8b
msgid "My radio setup isn't reading the RC channels right or hangs"
msgstr "我的遥控器设置无法正确读取 RC 通道或卡住了"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:167 7f2f7c1743534452a7b1edbc37299afc
msgid ""
"Click on that Calibrate Radio button. That will start the measurement "
"process."
msgstr "点击\"校准遥控器\"按钮，开始测量过程。"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:169 aaac55ce093e46a18ba4d08042dbb343
msgid ""
"Are you sure your receiver is getting power and is paired with your "
"transmitter (it should show a solid green light). Make sure your transmitter"
" is on!"
msgstr "您确定接收机已接通电源并与发射机配对了吗（应该显示稳定的绿灯）。确保您的发射机已开启！"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:172 6666863d198a450f896b60e34f1e5d41
msgid ""
"If you assembled the board yourself, double-check your soldering! A tiny "
"short on the APM board could disable all the channels."
msgstr "如果您是自己组装的板子，请仔细检查焊接！APM 板上的一个微小短路可能会禁用所有通道。"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:174 6277163face841e5bf221d43b8227806
msgid ""
"We've had some reports of problems with older FM RC gear and even the "
"occasional digital receiver, for reasons that are not clear (most likely low"
" voltage output). Can you try a different receiver? This at least will "
"eliminate that possibility."
msgstr ""
"我们收到一些关于旧 FM RC 设备甚至偶尔数字接收机出现问题的报告，原因不明（最可能是低电压输出）。您能尝试不同的接收机吗？这至少可以排除这一可能性。"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:178 8c48cb9771b8406db2b3c1ce6429a5dd
msgid ""
"We've also had reports of people having trouble with Spektrum radios, which "
"have a funky binding process. This is what works: To bind the receiver and "
"telemetry (TM1000+AR8000 to DX8) module, connect them both together(TM1000 "
"to AR8000). With the transmitter off (DX8 off), press the tiny button on the"
" side of the telemetry module (TM1000) and power the receiver (plug the LiPo"
" batteries but do not plug the 4-wire connection). Both the receiver and "
"telemetry module will start to blink (if they do not blink TM1000 is no "
"good). When that happens turn on your radio holding the trainer/bind button "
"and it will bind (stay at least 10ft away). Make sure that when it binds it "
"says something like \"binding dsmx ------ receiver with telemetry\". You may"
" have to do this twice if it doesn't pick up the telemetry module the first "
"time."
msgstr ""
"我们也收到过使用 Spektrum 遥控器遇到问题的报告，该遥控器有一个奇特的对频过程。以下方法有效：要对频接收机和数传（TM1000+AR8000 "
"连接到 DX8），将两者连接在一起（TM1000 连接到 AR8000）。在发射机关闭（DX8 "
"关闭）的情况下，按下数传模块（TM1000）侧面的小按钮，然后为接收机供电（插入 LiPo "
"电池，但不要插入四线连接）。接收机和数传模块都会开始闪烁（如果不闪烁，则 TM1000 有问题）。当发生这种情况时，按住 trainer/bind "
"按钮打开遥控器，它将完成对频（保持至少 10 英尺距离）。确保对频时显示类似\"binding dsmx ------ receiver with "
"telemetry\"的内容。如果第一次没有识别到数传模块，可能需要重复此过程两次。"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:191 36e8f2f55eba4acf88444dce9515c7be
msgid ""
"Check your cables! The signal wire should be at the top, and ground at the "
"bottom."
msgstr "检查您的线缆！信号线应在顶部，地线在底部。"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:193 7728497694404a2e9c6bc08b77b5faf0
msgid ""
"Finally, if all else fails, try to narrow down the problem. First, check "
"that the receiver is working right by plugging a servo into the output "
"you're testing and making sure that it's outputting a good signal. Then plug"
" one known-good RC channel into the APM input channels, from 1-7, one at a "
"time and see if any are read. If some channels are read and some are not, "
"you may have a soldering error or may have fried one or more inputs."
msgstr ""
"最后，如果一切都失败了，尝试缩小问题范围。首先，通过将舵机插入您正在测试的输出端来检查接收机是否正常工作，确保它输出良好信号。然后将一个已知良好的 RC"
" 通道依次插入 APM 输入通道 1-7，看看是否有任何通道被读取。如果某些通道被读取而另一些没有，您可能有焊接错误或烧坏了一个或多个输入端。"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:200 e809b80abfef41deb71487cec3fe2724
msgid ""
"If you still can't diagnose the problem, contact the customer support from "
"the store you bought it from."
msgstr "如果仍然无法诊断问题，请联系您购买产品的商店的客户支持。"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:204 1e62ad23312f4164962384e4dbee3bfc
msgid ""
"My Copter isn't as stable as I'd like or doesn't Loiter/Hold "
"Altitude/Navigate reliably"
msgstr "我的 Copter 不够稳定，或者无法可靠地 Loiter/保持高度/导航"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:206 876257b527264c50807a16c386c77d65
msgid ""
"Every copter is different, and even the official kit can have differences in"
" motor performance or balance depending on how you've put it together. So "
"we've made it relatively easy to tweak many of the performance settings to "
"turn your copter perfectly. That said, tuning is something of an art, so it "
"helps to read a bit more before you start tweaking."
msgstr ""
"每架 Copter 都不同，即使是官方套件，根据组装方式，电机性能或平衡性也可能有差异。因此，我们让调整许多性能设置变得相对容易，以使您的 Copter"
" 完美运行。话虽如此，调参是一门艺术，因此在开始调整之前多读一些内容会有所帮助。"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:213 3cccb0cdd0ee4dc7903ad3c0dbfae732
msgid "There is a guide to PID tuning \\ :ref:`here <tuning>`."
msgstr "这里有一份 PID 调参指南 \\ :ref:`此处 <tuning>`。"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:217 4d7a8804381e427996c5fb7da2e5092f
msgid "My Copter flies okay, but it tends to tilt one way or another"
msgstr "我的 Copter 飞行正常，但它倾向于向一个方向倾斜"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:219 a000af1b3a0f4b9894e7a82637f324ff
msgid ""
"Make sure the CG (center of gravity) of the copter is dead center. Then run "
"the level command on a flat surface. (hold disarm for ~15 seconds to "
"invoke.) You can also fly in auto-trim mode in a windless (important!) "
"environment--any wind will cause the changes you make to work against you "
"when the quad rotates 180°. Hold arm for ~ 20 seconds to fly in auto-trim "
"mode for about 45 seconds. It will exit auto-trim automatically and fly "
"normally. (Don't worry about counting out the time, just wait for the "
"flashing lights to enter either mode."
msgstr ""
"确保 Copter 的重心（CG）完全居中。然后在平坦的表面上运行水平命令。（按住上锁约 15 "
"秒以调用。）您也可以在无风（重要！）环境中以自动配平模式飞行——任何风都会在四轴旋转 180° 时使您所做的更改适得其反。按住解锁约 20 "
"秒以自动配平模式飞行约 45 秒。它将自动退出自动配平并正常飞行。（不必数时间，只需等待闪烁的灯进入任一模式即可。）"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:228 7b072f408ab744f9b79a503d4b3dac54
msgid ""
"You \\ **can** use your radio pitch and roll trims, but remember to re-"
"center them when you set up your radio with the config tools. I'm not a fan "
"of trimming the radio for quads, but NEVER, NEVER trim yaw. (Quads are also "
"susceptible to drafts. They will need constant correction unless you install"
" an optical flow sensor. One day...)"
msgstr ""
"您 \\ **可以** 使用遥控器的俯仰和横滚微调，但请记住在使用配置工具设置遥控器时将其重新居中。我不建议为四轴微调遥控器，但 **绝对不要** "
"微调偏航。（四轴也容易受到气流影响。除非安装光流传感器，否则需要持续校正。有一天会实现...）"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:235 5e9366b78e4747bfa1cdf283ddb85e86
msgid "My Copter Moves In a Direction even though the Stick is Centered"
msgstr "即使摇杆居中，我的 Copter 仍然向某个方向移动"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:237 6c72c8945d614ca1a9cd62edd4df650e
msgid ""
"It is very important that the RC Channel 1 and 2 Trim parameter values (for "
"the Roll and Pitch axes) are equal to the PWM value displayed in Mission "
"Planner for the stick in its center position during Radio Calibration."
msgstr ""
"RC 通道 1 和 2 的微调参数值（用于横滚和俯仰轴）必须等于在遥控器校准期间摇杆处于中心位置时 Mission Planner 中显示的 PWM "
"值，这一点非常重要。"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:242 35f9f71a67b640518877a4c1e7fd8418
msgid ""
"To check this Start Mission Planner, connect and go to the Advanced "
"Parameter List and write down the parameter for RC Trim PWM (HS1_TRIM) and "
"RC Trim PWM (HS2_TRIM)."
msgstr ""
"要检查此项，启动 Mission Planner，连接并进入高级参数列表，记下 RC Trim PWM (HS1_TRIM) 和 RC Trim PWM"
" (HS2_TRIM) 的参数。"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:245 ffb3a6edfd2c4edc92594beff486ecaa
msgid ""
"Now start up the radio Calibration function in Mission Planner and turn on "
"your RC Transmitter."
msgstr "现在在 Mission Planner 中启动遥控器校准功能并打开您的 RC 遥控器。"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:247 023ed3ab3f2c4880ac2de76ad4428c5d
msgid ""
"With the Roll and Pitch Stick centered, the values of the channel 1 (roll) "
"and channel 2 (pitch) PWMs should be the same as the values for the "
"parameters you wrote down above."
msgstr "将横滚和俯仰摇杆居中后，通道 1（横滚）和通道 2（俯仰）PWM 的值应与您上面记下的参数值相同。"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:250 6ac01467f40d4e2bae64df8abb50d8a4
msgid "If they are not recalibrate the radio."
msgstr "如果不一致，请重新校准遥控器。"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:251 6480a7c896c647d5980d5ca20e0cbeb1
msgid ""
"The HS1 Trim value must match the Live stick centered Roll value and the HS2"
" Trim value must match the live stick centered Pitch value or the autopilot "
"will think your stick is not centered when it is."
msgstr "HS1 微调值必须与实时摇杆居中横滚值匹配，HS2 微调值必须与实时摇杆居中俯仰值匹配，否则飞控会认为您的摇杆不在中心位置。"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:256 e9f253f0151d4ae6b5c5ab1718cedabc
msgid "Make sure the CG (center of gravity) of the copter is dead center."
msgstr "确保 Copter 的重心（CG）完全居中。"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:257 ffe8ebc5deee434db97a61dd71d7fe37
msgid ""
"Then run the level command on a flat surface. (hold disarm for ~15 seconds "
"to invoke.)"
msgstr "然后在平坦的表面上运行水平命令。（按住上锁约 15 秒以调用。）"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:260 d494a3eff162404d81fc100c40096946
msgid ""
"You can also fly in auto-trim mode in a windless (important!) environment--"
"any wind will cause the changes you make to work against you when the quad "
"rotates 180°."
msgstr "您也可以在无风（重要！）环境中以自动配平模式飞行——任何风都会在四轴旋转 180° 时使您所做的更改适得其反。"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:263 1f9f8503d26e4ea0a4d033a2d73e1287
msgid ""
"Hold arm for ~ 20 seconds to fly in auto-trim mode for about 45 seconds."
msgstr "按住解锁约 20 秒以自动配平模式飞行约 45 秒。"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:265 c2db47006ebb49b5be4d456f4cdb7966
msgid ""
"It will exit auto-trim automatically and fly normally. (Don't worry about "
"counting out the time, just wait for the flashing lights to enter either "
"mode."
msgstr "它将自动退出自动配平并正常飞行。（不必数时间，只需等待闪烁的灯进入任一模式即可。）"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:269 9f16b39060ea49cab71818c5d76540b2
msgid ""
"Avoid it if possible but if you have to you can use some radio pitch and "
"roll trims"
msgstr "如果可能请避免，但如果必须，您可以使用遥控器的俯仰和横滚微调"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:271 23d6717d6a8441bd861a313089d5c63b
msgid "NEVER use any radio trim for Yaw."
msgstr "绝对不要对偏航使用任何遥控器微调。"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:274 de68d20777884d878047106d748845ef
msgid "The quad always wants to yaw to the right or left when I take off"
msgstr "起飞时四轴总是向右或向左偏航"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:276 6278431eb07e46d09be5a7bfe0c9c45e
msgid ""
"This is usually due to an airframe that it out of tune, either with one "
"motor tilted slightly or the weight balance not centered. Typically, the bad"
" behavior is that the quad will always yaw by a certain amount, typically "
"around 30-45 degrees on takeoff, but will stay in that direction. This is "
"because the mechanical asymmetry of an out-of-tune quad is forcing the yaw, "
"and the limit is just how long it take for the P term in the AC2's PID "
"equations to grow and stop it."
msgstr ""
"这通常是由于机架未调整好，可能是某个电机轻微倾斜或重量平衡不居中。典型的不良行为是四轴起飞时总会偏航一定角度，通常约为 30-45 "
"度，但会保持在该方向。这是因为未调整好的四轴的机械不对称性强制产生偏航，而极限就是 AC2 PID 方程中的 P 项增长并停止它所需的时间。"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:284 026d44df0cb345ac9741175f7993e8e1
msgid ""
"Although you can adjust those terms in the Mission Planner's PID "
"configuration screen, the best solution is to solve it at the source. "
"Eyeball each motor and see if it or the arm it is one is slightly tilted, "
"and bend it back to vertical if so. Also ensure that the battery is centered"
" on the quad and the center of gravity of the vehicle is as close to the "
"center of the APM board as possible. It's also a great idea to redo the ESC "
"calibration routine just in case."
msgstr ""
"尽管您可以在 Mission Planner 的 PID "
"配置屏幕中调整这些参数，但最佳解决方案是从根源解决。目视检查每个电机，看它或其所在的臂是否轻微倾斜，如有则将其弯回垂直。同时确保电池居中放置，飞行器的重心尽可能接近"
" APM 板的中心。重新进行 ESC 校准程序也是个好主意。"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:292 031c91c783874aa1a2f510368d274c8e
msgid ""
"Also make sure that you've got your forward-rotating and counter-rotating "
"props on the right motors, as shown \\ :ref:`here <connect-escs-and-"
"motors_attach_propellers>`."
msgstr ""
"同时确保您的正转和反转螺旋桨安装在正确的电机上，如 \\ :ref:`此处 <connect-escs-and-"
"motors_attach_propellers>` 所示。"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:297 3a85a59a396747dd981758b0e60f1532
msgid "The quad always wants to yaw when I pitch or roll"
msgstr "当我俯仰或横滚时四轴总是偏航"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:299 158a0f933ba548fcb2021196bad814d3
msgid ""
"Your compass may need calibrating. AC2 calibrates while flying to take the "
"magnetic fields of your motors into account. You must disarm the motors at "
"the end of your flight to save your calibration to EEPROM. It usually takes "
"1-2 flights before the calibration makes a difference."
msgstr ""
"您的罗盘可能需要校准。AC2 在飞行中进行校准，以考虑电机磁场的影响。您必须在飞行结束时上锁电机，以将校准保存到 EEPROM。通常需要 1-2 "
"次飞行后校准才能产生效果。"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:304 fc46d3e581274a1b929699bb8551443a
msgid ""
"You must use a compass in conjunction with a GPS. If you disable your "
"compass, please disconnect your GPS or you will have random Yaw hold issue."
msgstr "您必须将罗盘与 GPS 配合使用。如果您禁用罗盘，请断开 GPS，否则会出现随机的偏航保持问题。"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:309 c6ef2efe386843c8b8fb18b01e41b8b1
msgid ""
"My copter flies well, but then dips a motor arm in a fidgety manner while "
"hovering"
msgstr "我的 Copter 飞行良好，但在悬停时某个电机臂会断断续续地下沉"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:311 e8f65b97438d416c831e6c6674bf9408
msgid ""
"The most likely cause of this is your bullet connectors. After your initial "
"setup, when you test motor direction and electrical connections, we\\ "
"**strongly** recommend that you cut off the bullet connectors and directly "
"solder the motors wires to the ESC wires. That way is vibration-proof and "
"will lead to much more reliable operation."
msgstr ""
"这最可能的原因是子弹头连接器。在初始设置完成后，当您测试电机方向和电气连接时，我们 **强烈** 建议您剪断子弹头连接器，直接将电机线焊接到 ESC "
"线上。这样可以防震，并会带来更可靠的操作。"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:317 b1a338884bcd48e493148bddc7b8da99
msgid ""
"If your wires are soldered without bullet connectors and you still see this "
"issue, there are some other things that can cause this problem. Your motor "
"may be going bad: either the bearings are going or your shaft is horribly "
"bent. A motor with bad bearings takes more power to spin. In that situation,"
" the ESC could be cutting out to protect itself. Or it maybe flying slow "
"enough to stall the motor. Attach a current sensor between your battery and "
"the motor and test the difference between a good motor and the bad one. If "
"you are seeing higher draw in the bad one, replace or fix it."
msgstr ""
"如果您的线已焊接而没有子弹头连接器，仍然看到此问题，还有其他一些原因可能导致此问题。您的电机可能正在损坏：轴承故障或轴严重弯曲。轴承损坏的电机需要更多功率才能旋转。在这种情况下，ESC"
" "
"可能会切断以保护自身，或者可能旋转太慢而导致电机失速。在电池和电机之间连接电流传感器，测试好电机和坏电机之间的差异。如果坏电机的电流消耗更高，请更换或修复它。"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:328 b7189336de6b4270a8b5b89e087b002f
msgid ""
"Another possible cause is the THR_MIN parameter's default of 130 is too low "
"for your motors or ESCs. The THR_MIN parameter controls the minimum throttle"
" that will be sent to the ESCs/motors to ensure they keep spinning while "
"your throttle is above zero. If this parameter is too low it is possible for"
" your motors to momentarily stop leading to a twitch. Try increasing this "
"parameter to 150. You should be careful not to set this parameter too high "
"(i.e. >150 especially on a high powered copter)."
msgstr ""
"另一个可能的原因是 THR_MIN 参数的默认值 130 对您的电机或 ESC 来说太低。THR_MIN 参数控制发送给 "
"ESC/电机的最低油门，确保它们在油门高于零时持续旋转。如果此参数过低，您的电机可能会瞬间停止，导致抖动。尝试将此参数增加到 "
"150。应注意不要将此参数设置得过高（即对于高功率 Copter 不要超过 150）。"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:340 177a034d557646729888d92a88c3f6c9
msgid "One of my motors started shaking and then burned out!"
msgstr "我的一个电机开始颤抖，然后烧坏了！"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:342 d17e3410bfa64d979f09c41c98bf23ff
msgid ""
"Motors will typically twitch once per second or so (often with a beep) while"
" they're waiting for a signal. That's normal. But sometimes, if you have not"
" followed the warnings and disconnected the four-wire signal cable, they may"
" vibrate rapidly when you reset your board. This is a rare problem that can "
"crop up with certain ESC types that don't handle out-of-range signals well "
"(it's a problem with the Arduino bootloader during boot-up, so there's not "
"much we can do about it). But it can always be avoided by following the "
"advice of this warning, which is liberally sprinkled throughout the manual!"
msgstr ""
"电机在等待信号时通常每秒抖动一次左右（通常伴随蜂鸣声），这是正常的。但有时，如果您没有按照警告断开四线信号线，在重置飞控板时它们可能会快速震动。这是一个罕见的问题，可能出现在某些无法正常处理超范围信号的电调类型上（这是"
" Arduino 引导程序在启动期间的问题，我们对此无能为力）。但只要遵循本手册中多处提及的这一警告，始终可以避免此问题！"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:353 92df58d3b1734a0daa0060d71d1e02bb
msgid ""
"The APM board works when it's plugged into the USB, but not when it's "
"powered by the RC rail (ESC/Lipo)"
msgstr "APM 板通过 USB 连接时可以工作，但通过 RC 总线（ESC/Lipo）供电时无法工作"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:355 6063400e31824858a78fa7c6301d865b
msgid ""
"APM allows for both RC power or a separate battery run through APM's built-"
"in power regulator as described \\ :ref:`here <common-"
"apm25-and-26-overview>`. A solder jumper called SJ1 determines which is "
"used. By default from the factory, that jumper should be soldered which "
"means APM will be powered by the RC rail."
msgstr ""
"APM 允许通过 RC 电源或通过 APM 内置电压调节器的独立电池供电，如 \\ :ref:`此处 <common-"
"apm25-and-26-overview>` 所述。一个名为 SJ1 的焊接跳线决定使用哪种方式。出厂默认情况下，该跳线应该已焊接，这意味着 APM "
"将由 RC 总线供电。"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:362 aae355ca66b348ba853f5a7d0d52db2e
msgid ""
"If for some reason, connecting power to the RC rail does not power your "
"board, check to see if that jumper is soldered. If it isn't, as shown below,"
" just solder a blob of solder over the two pads to connect them."
msgstr ""
"如果由于某种原因，向 RC 总线接通电源无法为您的板供电，请检查该跳线是否已焊接。如果未焊接（如下图所示），只需在两个焊盘上焊上一团焊锡将它们连接即可。"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:370 6dc34403791f4c698838da2383ac872c
msgid ""
"In the \"raw sensor view\" of the Mission Planner, the Z accelerometer "
"reading is always 1000, not 0, when it's on the bench"
msgstr "在 Mission Planner 的\"原始传感器视图\"中，Z 轴加速度计读数在放置于桌面时始终为 1000 而不是 0"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:372 4e7e6385cdbf487bbea6512e5c7acba5
msgid ""
"That's normal. The Z accelerometer is showing the force of gravity (which is"
" an acceleration, as you'll recall from high school physics). If you turn "
"the quad upside down, you'll see that it reverses."
msgstr "这是正常的。Z 轴加速度计显示的是重力加速度（您会记得高中物理中这是一种加速度）。如果您将四轴翻转过来，您会看到数值反向。"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:377 70096945c3364e16b972d45517e354f8
msgid "I can't connect with the Mission Planner over Xbee"
msgstr "我无法通过 Xbee 与 Mission Planner 连接"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:379 c69fc4580713461d9ae56cb0a0e0ace2
msgid ""
"First, remember that you cannot use wireless telemetry with APM 2 while the "
"USB cable is plugged in (they use the same port). Make sure it's unplugged."
msgstr "首先，请记住在插入 USB 线缆时无法使用无线数传与 APM 2 通信（它们使用同一端口）。确保已拔出 USB 线缆。"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:383 7bea7b367b16410cb0d22c6e30ee6972
msgid ""
"Check that you've switching the Mission Planner to the COM port assigned to "
"your Xbee that's connected to your PC and set the baud rate to 57600."
msgstr "检查您是否已将 Mission Planner 切换到分配给连接到 PC 的 Xbee 的 COM 端口，并将波特率设置为 57600。"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:386 c97447b0a1814461a2ace001a3b3f43c
msgid ""
"Ensure that you've gone through the full Xbee configuration process "
"described \\ :ref:`here. <common-telemetry-xbee>` Run the test code at the "
"bottom of that page to ensure that your Xbees are communicating. \\ "
"**Remember that the Xbees must be programmed in X-CTU to run at 57k.**"
msgstr ""
"确保您已完成 \\ :ref:`此处 <common-telemetry-xbee>` 描述的完整 Xbee "
"配置过程。运行该页面底部的测试代码，以确保您的 Xbee 正在通信。\\ **请记住，Xbee 必须在 X-CTU 中编程为以 57k 运行。**"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:392 2af6ccadf0e64af6ad5f73bec9dfb672
msgid ""
"If your Xbees suddenly stop working, it could be that a loose cable has led "
"to a signal glitch that bricked the airborne one."
msgstr "如果您的 Xbee 突然停止工作，可能是松动的线缆导致信号故障，使机载 Xbee 变砖。"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:396 78404d70d40d4fdbb601e63597aac16d
msgid "I can't connect with the Mission Planner with the 3DR Radios"
msgstr "我无法通过 3DR Radio 与 Mission Planner 连接"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:398 84af1ff0e28d4a3f99fccbdde973caa5
msgid ""
"Remember that you cannot use wireless telemetry with APM 2 while the USB "
"cable is plugged in (they use the same port). Make sure it's unplugged."
msgstr "请记住在插入 USB 线缆时无法使用无线数传与 APM 2 通信（它们使用同一端口）。确保已拔出 USB 线缆。"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:401 a8b1f1b0b6174db38bb0c805d33306c8
msgid ""
"Check that you've switching the Mission Planner to the COM port assigned to "
"your 3DR radio that's connected to your PC and set the baud rate to 57600."
msgstr "检查您是否已将 Mission Planner 切换到分配给连接到 PC 的 3DR 数传的 COM 端口，并将波特率设置为 57600。"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:406 936bc9e0166647419bcc001361b3c704
msgid "I'm having trouble connecting via MAVLink over USB"
msgstr "我在通过 USB 使用 MAVLink 连接时遇到问题"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:408 822554b75a6a401d8d04771b5216ecb8
msgid ""
"Double check that you've selected the right COM port and baud rate for USB "
"(115200). Also double check in your Windows Device Manager which COM port "
"your APM has been assigned to. It will be listed under Ports."
msgstr ""
"再次检查您是否为 USB 选择了正确的 COM 端口和波特率（115200）。同时在 Windows 设备管理器中检查您的 APM 被分配到哪个 COM"
" 端口，它将列在\"端口\"下。"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:412 c1940e1e71a3410d803f2baa2043b80a
msgid ""
"Did you use the MP installation program, which installs the drivers, and did"
" it complete successfully?"
msgstr "您是否使用了 MP 安装程序（该程序会安装驱动程序），并且安装是否成功完成？"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:414 810e930ebb594db38df030f3ebe9ab9b
msgid "Have you loaded flight firmware (Copter or Plane) to APM?"
msgstr "您是否已将飞行固件（Copter 或 Plane）加载到 APM？"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:415 f05ad2bee12a49539a3d811694bcacf1
msgid "Did you press Connect in the MP?"
msgstr "您是否在 MP 中按下了\"连接\"按钮？"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:418 03686ed7085942a8acb005f4b04ad774
msgid "Copter ESCs keep beeping"
msgstr "Copter ESC 持续发出蜂鸣声"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:420 f3f20b2ea7dc4ada8f686480dcee235f
msgid "Have you set up your RC input in the Mission Planner setup process?"
msgstr "您是否在 Mission Planner 设置过程中设置了 RC 输入？"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:421 164e9ace7fd14c179748cfb1da39c7a4
msgid ""
"Check that your RC radio is talking properly to its receiver (typically, "
"that will be shown by a green light on the receiver)."
msgstr "检查您的 RC 遥控器是否与接收机正常通信（通常，接收机上的绿灯常亮表示正常）。"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:423 b001a56ad4c0489ca0cc739f4778ce31
msgid ""
"If those two check out, you probably just need to calibrate your ESCs (even "
"if you've done that before, if you've erased your EEPROM and done a reset, "
"you'll need to do it again. It's an easy procedure and the instructions are "
"\\ :ref:`here. <esc-calibration>`"
msgstr ""
"如果以上两项检查通过，您可能只需要校准 ESC（即使您之前已经做过，如果您已清除 EEPROM 并重置，则需要重新执行。这是一个简单的过程，说明在 \\"
" :ref:`此处 <esc-calibration>`）。"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:428 525c914d040c43d18b187172d7befb55
msgid ""
"Check that your radio channels are in right order (cabling and/or Mode-1, "
"Mode-2)"
msgstr "检查您的遥控器通道顺序是否正确（线缆和/或 Mode-1、Mode-2）"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:438 5a8548e72d934e34813d758ab352dd37
msgid ""
"I'm using a MediaTek GPS, and although the module's blue lock LED goes "
"solid, APM is not showing a lock or I'm getting \"No GPS\" on the Mission "
"Planner display"
msgstr ""
"我正在使用 MediaTek GPS，虽然模块的蓝色锁定 LED 常亮，但 APM 未显示锁定，或者在 Mission Planner "
"显示屏上出现\"No GPS\""

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:440 7d35eef38dbf4576b4140ae4efde5d90
msgid "I'm also not getting GPS data in my telemetry."
msgstr "我的数传中也没有 GPS 数据。"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:442 8a2f8edefde24e709f7d4858809cc7d9
msgid "Solution:"
msgstr "解决方案："

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:444 b43036d7ac244a909a978bd74db12a64
msgid ""
"There are a few things that could cause this. First, make sure that your "
"input voltage to APM is not too high. It should be in the range 5-5.4v. \\ "
"**Do not power the board at 6v.**"
msgstr "这可能由几个原因引起。首先，确保 APM 的输入电压不太高。应在 5-5.4v 范围内。\\ **请勿以 6v 为板供电。**"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:448 3685e8ebde2d4f91bc01f5ec19629a59
msgid ""
"Second, ensure that you've selected the right MediaTek version in the config"
" file. If you bought your module from the DIY Drones store before December, "
"2010, it had version 1.0 firmware: select GPS_PROTOCOL_MTK in the config "
"file. If you bought it after that, it as version 1.6 firmware: select "
"GPS_PROTOCOL_MTK16 in the config file."
msgstr ""
"其次，确保您在配置文件中选择了正确的 MediaTek 版本。如果您在 2010 年 12 月之前从 DIY Drones 商店购买了模块，它使用 "
"1.0 版固件：在配置文件中选择 GPS_PROTOCOL_MTK。如果是之后购买的，则使用 1.6 版固件：在配置文件中选择 "
"GPS_PROTOCOL_MTK16。"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:454 66a49777d26b4c2aadd2ffc1b2ab030d
msgid ""
"Finally, if things still aren't working, check your cable. Cables longer "
"than the short one that ships with the GPS module tend to have thinner wires"
" that can break."
msgstr "最后，如果问题仍然存在，请检查您的线缆。比 GPS 模块附带的短线缆更长的线缆往往有更细的导线，容易断裂。"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:459 39521d81f60d47f8955741d1823bbeba
msgid "I'm not getting GPS lock at all"
msgstr "我根本无法获得 GPS 锁定"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:461 b195309623534127a5a7b6d80aed8907
msgid ""
"First, note that you will probably only get GPS lock outside (if you're very"
" near a window or are lucky enough to have strong GPS signal and a radio-"
"transparent roof, you may be able to get lock inside). For a cold start "
"(power on), it make take three minutes or more. If you're just hitting the "
"reset button after lock has been achieved, it should take less than a "
"minute."
msgstr ""
"首先，请注意您可能只有在室外才能获得 GPS 锁定（如果您非常靠近窗户，或者足够幸运地有强 GPS "
"信号和射频透明屋顶，您可能能够在室内获得锁定）。冷启动（上电）可能需要三分钟或更长时间。如果您只是在已获得锁定后按下重置按钮，则应该在一分钟内完成。"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:468 d8b959e0acb04bb2b3efe1ecdc06fd15
msgid ""
"If you can't get GPS lock outside after many minutes(the blue LED on the "
"MediaTek module keeps blinking), you may have a defective module. If the "
"module shows lock, but the red APM GPS LED is still blinking, you either "
"have a bad cable or an older MediaTek module that needs to have its firmware"
" updated."
msgstr ""
"如果您在室外等待多分钟后仍无法获得 GPS 锁定（MediaTek 模块的蓝色 LED 持续闪烁），您可能有一个故障模块。如果模块显示锁定，但 APM "
"的红色 GPS LED 仍在闪烁，则您可能有一根损坏的线缆，或者是一个较旧的 MediaTek 模块需要更新固件。"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:474 b671f048ad514066bdd4828a369610f7
msgid ""
"If you have a uBlox module and APM is not showing lock, you may not have "
"ordered the module preprogrammed for ArduPilot from the DIY Drones store "
"(you had to select that option). In that case, program it yourself with the "
"instructions `here <https://diydrones.com/profiles/blogs/tutorial-"
"programming-your>`__."
msgstr ""
"如果您有 uBlox 模块，APM 未显示锁定，您可能没有从 DIY Drones 商店订购预先为 ArduPilot "
"编程的模块（您需要选择该选项）。在这种情况下，请按照 `此处 "
"<https://diydrones.com/profiles/blogs/tutorial-programming-your>`__ 的说明自行编程。"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:481 3d1d0f8060994268ab5c12558110f794
msgid "I want to load the code in Arduino, but I'm having trouble"
msgstr "我想在 Arduino 中加载代码，但遇到了问题"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:483 7c92402f0e3c462299d5535f1e9f6d48
msgid ""
"First, ensure you've downloaded the latest AC2 code and are using the latest"
" Arduino (at least 022)."
msgstr "首先，确保您已下载最新的 AC2 代码并使用最新版本的 Arduino（至少 022）。"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:486 922a4e21fa294de0acaa8a44ca3d9ab2
msgid ""
"If you're getting compile errors, that means that you haven't told Arduino "
"where your libraries are properly."
msgstr "如果您遇到编译错误，这意味着您没有正确告诉 Arduino 库的位置。"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:488 64f7ad8628c24f64950157c9a520a980
msgid ""
"If you're getting avrdude sync error message in the Arduino status bar), go "
"through *all* of the tips `here "
"<https://diydrones.com/profiles/blogs/arduino-debugging-tips>`__."
msgstr ""
"如果您在 Arduino 状态栏中看到 avrdude 同步错误消息，请按照 `此处 "
"<https://diydrones.com/profiles/blogs/arduino-debugging-tips>`__ 的*所有*技巧操作。"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:492 b773794d9b2e4d588d781bf538362c57
msgid "My Copter just won't rise/lift off"
msgstr "我的 Copter 就是无法起飞"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:494 30fa53e9a01a45f891e2d62d075d58cc
msgid ""
"If you have a problems on getting your Copter up from the ground, check that"
" you propellers are mounted correct way."
msgstr "如果您的 Copter 无法从地面起飞，请检查螺旋桨是否以正确方式安装。"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:497 3846cde2de8b43c8b1cea53c46d7f407
msgid ""
"Official Copter propellers are not symmetric and they need to be mounted "
"proper way. If you look close to center mounting hole, there are small texts"
" saying 10x45 or 12x45. There texts needs to be upside."
msgstr ""
"官方 Copter 螺旋桨不是对称的，需要以正确方式安装。如果您仔细查看中心安装孔附近，会看到标有 10x45 或 12x45 "
"的小字。这些文字需要朝上。"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:501 15078f8420424eabb11a73a925832781
msgid "If text is on downside, your Copter cannot lift properly."
msgstr "如果文字朝下，您的 Copter 就无法正常起飞。"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:503 486446e89db849bdb9bd81d7137cc35a
msgid ""
"The props that came with early version of the 3D Robotics Copter were also "
"of uneven quality and some would flex too much under load, reducing lift. If"
" you have these (black and more flexible than most props), you should "
"replace them with APC or equivalent props or contact 3D Robotics for a "
"replacement."
msgstr ""
"3D Robotics Copter "
"早期版本附带的螺旋桨质量也参差不齐，有些在负载下会过度弯曲，降低升力。如果您有这些（黑色且比大多数螺旋桨更柔软的），应将其更换为 APC "
"或同等螺旋桨，或联系 3D Robotics 进行更换。"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:510 5d25463a97d2439cb053103af6801d7b
msgid "My Copter feels sloppy on roll or pitch axis"
msgstr "我的 Copter 在横滚或俯仰轴上感觉松散"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:512 1effa9a9cbc04558972288e4312b590d
msgid ""
"Both of roll and pitch axis should give to you exact or close to similar "
"response when doing hand tests. If one of the axis does not respond as "
"expected, check your PID settings and you can try to upload firmware again."
msgstr ""
"横滚和俯仰两个轴在进行手持测试时应该给出完全相同或非常相似的响应。如果其中一个轴的响应不符合预期，请检查您的 PID 设置，也可以尝试重新上传固件。"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:517 6fc7661628784a92984b35e7f0937ec2
msgid ""
"Firmware upload might be successful but due internal timing issues some of "
"the code is not written properly and this can cause unstableness on your "
"Copter."
msgstr "固件上传可能成功，但由于内部时序问题，部分代码未能正确写入，这可能导致您的 Copter 不稳定。"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:522 3c6577c8fb08467b93606d1d57d8686a
msgid "I've got a tricopter and I'm having trouble with the yaw"
msgstr "我有一架三旋翼飞机，偏航出现问题"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:524 6f264fe8c02744d091291e5927c037e2
msgid ""
"Please see the tips `here <https://diydrones.com/profiles/blogs/tricopter-"
"based-on-arducopter-yaw-issues-and-solutions>`__."
msgstr ""
"请参阅 `此处 <https://diydrones.com/profiles/blogs/tricopter-based-on-arducopter-"
"yaw-issues-and-solutions>`__ 的技巧。"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:527 40fca5eaede6413daf31229a809d3728
msgid ""
"The Mission Planner's HUD display moves around even though my copter is "
"motionless"
msgstr "Mission Planner 的 HUD 显示在我的 Copter 静止时仍在移动"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:529 5617a3cf0c91449caa9aa322c5a71ce8
msgid ""
"As of 2.9 we've enabled a feature that uses GPS velocities/accelerations to "
"compensate for centrifugal forces. It should not cause you any issues in "
"flight but you can disable it by setting the AHRS_GPS_GAIN to 0 through the "
"Mission Planner's Advanced Parameters List if it makes you uncomfortable. \\"
" `Here is a video "
"<https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=SXppOmZ3Rpg&feature=player_detailpage>`__ "
"demonstrating the problem and the explanation as to why it happens."
msgstr ""
"从 2.9 版本起，我们启用了一项使用 GPS 速度/加速度来补偿离心力的功能。这在飞行中不应该给您带来任何问题，但如果您感到不舒适，可以通过 "
"Mission Planner 的高级参数列表将 AHRS_GPS_GAIN 设置为 0 来禁用它。\\ `此处有一个视频 "
"<https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=SXppOmZ3Rpg&feature=player_detailpage>`__ "
"演示了该问题及其发生原因的解释。"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:537 48ab412f32bf4c0a88c9ebada49b9e08
msgid ""
"My copter's is moving a lot on the Mission Planner map even though it's "
"sitting still in my house"
msgstr "我的 Copter 在 Mission Planner 地图上大幅移动，尽管它静止地放在我家里"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:539 972167eaadd94cca894f127cf886ebd4
msgid ""
"a GPS will rarely give an accurate position while indoors or near walls due "
"to multipath-ing. If you go outside you should see that it settles down."
msgstr "在室内或靠近墙壁时，GPS 很少能给出准确的位置，这是由于多径效应。如果您去室外，应该会看到它稳定下来。"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:547 fa1e1706d13a491581c3c2996d176de1
msgid ""
"In Alt-Hold or loiter my copter is very bouncy or takes off into the sky"
msgstr "在 AltHold 或 Loiter 模式下，我的 Copter 剧烈颠簸或飞向天空"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:549 43e312f69edf401e80ac586761f949e4
msgid ""
"Copter uses the accelerometers heavily for calculating altitude and climb "
"rate. Vibrations from the motors can cause the accelerometer values to "
"become very noisy and throw off the altitude estimates. The solution is to "
"reduce sources of vibration from your frame (bent prop adapters and motor "
"shafts, replace EPP props with APC) and remove hard connections between the "
"frame and APM by using vibration dampening products such as \\ `DuBro foam "
"<https://www.dubro.com/products/r-c-protective-foam-rubber>`__."
msgstr ""
"Copter "
"大量使用加速度计来计算高度和爬升率。电机引起的震动可能导致加速度计数值变得非常嘈杂，从而影响高度估算。解决方案是减少来自机架的震动源（弯曲的螺旋桨适配器和电机轴、用"
" APC 螺旋桨替换 EPP 螺旋桨），并通过使用震动阻尼产品（如 \\ `DuBro 泡沫 "
"<https://www.dubro.com/products/r-c-protective-foam-rubber>`__）消除机架与 APM "
"之间的硬连接。"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:557 eef4397a6a9441e08377e9721aa26eef
msgid ""
"As of version 2.9 of Copter, inertial navigation is used to maintain "
"altitude and in 2.9.2 horizontal position as well so vibration truly needs "
"to be minimized. A small pad (1/2 to 1\") of Kyosho Zeal tape under each "
"corner of the autopilot should get vibration low enough."
msgstr ""
"从 Copter 2.9 版本起，惯性导航用于保持高度，在 2.9.2 "
"版本中还用于保持水平位置，因此震动真的需要最小化。在飞控每个角落下面贴一小块（1/2 到 1 英寸）Kyosho Zeal "
"胶带应该可以将震动降至足够低。"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:562 0107323b898a473eb5d0ddfbbdf89c6a
msgid ""
"Or you can use a standoff with an extending screw 1/10\" outboard of each "
"corner of the autopilot and suspend it with four 1/16\" O-rings of "
"appropriate diameter such that when folded over through the autopilot they "
"just hold the board without movement, but also not in much tension."
msgstr ""
"或者，您可以在飞控每个角落外侧 1/10 英寸处使用带延长螺丝的支柱，并用直径适当的四个 1/16 英寸 O "
"形圈悬挂它，使其折叠穿过飞控时恰好固定住板而不晃动，但也不会有太大张力。"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:568 07d961d7ff574e258eceba47895b2f05
msgid ""
"When a flight log is checked in RAW mode, X,Y and Z hovering ACCELs "
"vibration on a log graph should at least be in the + to - 5 range and either"
" of the above techniques can get them down to the plus to minus 1 range if "
"they are just right."
msgstr ""
"当在 RAW 模式下查看飞行日志时，日志图表上悬停时的 X、Y 和 Z 轴 ACCEL 震动至少应在 + 到 - 5 "
"的范围内，上述两种技术在调整得恰当时都可以将其降至正负 1 的范围。"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:573 753cef6617234054947948de54765b80
msgid ""
"You can graph your Z-axis vibrations by enabling the \"RAW\" message type in"
" the :ref:`dataflash <common-downloading-and-analyzing-data-logs-in-mission-"
"planner>`, then take a short flight in Stabilize mode and finally download "
"the logs and graph them with the mission planner. Below is an example of an "
"extremely badly vibrating copter (top) and a nearly perfectly smooth copter "
"(bottom). The Z-axis vibrations should not move up and down more than -5 to "
"-15 or alt hold will not function correctly."
msgstr ""
"您可以通过在 :ref:`dataflash <common-downloading-and-analyzing-data-logs-in-"
"mission-planner>` 中启用\"RAW\"消息类型来绘制 Z 轴震动图，然后在 Stabilize 模式下进行短暂飞行，最后下载日志并在 "
"Mission Planner 中绘制图表。以下是一个极度震动的 Copter（上图）和一个几乎完全平滑的 Copter（下图）的示例。Z "
"轴震动不应超过 -5 至 -15 的范围，否则高度保持将无法正常运作。"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:584 fba66df897a94edc814786f759bfa348
msgid ""
"There is a good discussion `here "
"<https://diydrones.com/forum/topics/vibration-isolation-and-dampening-of-"
"apm-px4-for-version-2-9>`__ re vibration dampening."
msgstr ""
"这里有一个关于震动阻尼的 `讨论 <https://diydrones.com/forum/topics/vibration-isolation-"
"and-dampening-of-apm-px4-for-version-2-9>`__。"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:587 b82d726b7eb34d58a7cfcd31f6f718c6
msgid "My copter slowly rises or descends when I enable Alt-Hold or Loiter"
msgstr "当我启用 AltHold 或 Loiter 时，我的 Copter 缓慢上升或下降"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:589 f6ab61ec0d9d41e18c35af23001ee7ae
#, no-python-format
msgid ""
"The throttle deadband when in alt-hold or loiter mode is from 40% ~ 60% of "
"the throttle. If you have an overpowered or underpowered copter then when in"
" stabilize mode the throttle required to maintain a hover may be outside "
"this range. So when you engage alt-hold or loiter your throttle is outside "
"of the deadband and Copter thinks you want to climb or descend. The simple "
"solution is to move your throttle back to centre as you engage alt-hold. A "
"permanent solution is to modify the THR_MID parameter through the mission "
"planner's Adv Parameter List screen. If your copter hover at 40% of throttle"
" stick when in stabilize mode, make THR_MID = 400. If it hovers at 60% of "
"throttle make the parameter 600, etc."
msgstr ""
"在 AltHold 或 Loiter 模式下，油门死区为油门的 40%~60%。如果您的 Copter 动力过强或不足，在 Stabilize "
"模式下保持悬停所需的油门可能超出此范围。因此，当您切换到 AltHold 或 Loiter 时，您的油门在死区之外，Copter "
"认为您想要爬升或下降。简单的解决方案是在切换到 AltHold 时将油门移回中心。永久解决方案是通过 Mission Planner "
"的高级参数列表屏幕修改 THR_MID 参数。如果您的 Copter 在 Stabilize 模式下以油门 40% 悬停，设置 THR_MID = "
"400。如果以 60% 油门悬停，设置参数为 600，以此类推。"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:602 85e308bbce7943f489c9d00a054b339f
msgid "Mission planner displays enormous \"Distance to Home\" or \"Dist to WP\""
msgstr "Mission Planner 显示巨大的\"到 Home 的距离\"或\"到航点的距离\""

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:604 5ba25a710fca43408d015ab92eedf0a1
msgid ""
"The \"Dist to WP\" (distance to waypoint) default to -1 when you do not have"
" a waypoint set. Because of a display issue the mission planner displays "
"this negative number as 65535. It will display a proper number as soon as "
"you enter loiter mode, guided more or start a mission. This display issue "
"will be fixed in a future version of Copter."
msgstr ""
"当您没有设置航点时，\"到航点的距离\"(Dist to WP) 默认为 -1。由于显示问题，Mission Planner 将这个负数显示为 "
"65535。一旦进入 Loiter 模式、引导模式或开始任务，它将显示正确的数字。此显示问题将在 Copter 的未来版本中修复。"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:610 bb0fd148075e4a45a1e95d923f539192
msgid ""
"The \"Distance to Home\" is the distance from the mission planner's home "
"location (which is different from the Copter's home location which is set "
"when you arm the motors). You can reset the mission planner's home location "
"to the copter's current location by clicking on the \"Home Location\" link "
"in the Flight Planner screen. Below is a video explanation and how resolve "
"it."
msgstr ""
"\"到 Home 的距离\"是 Mission Planner 的 Home 位置（不同于 Copter 的 Home "
"位置，后者是在解锁电机时设置的）到当前位置的距离。您可以通过在飞行计划屏幕中点击\"Home Location\"链接将 Mission Planner"
" 的 Home 位置重置为 Copter 的当前位置。以下是视频说明及解决方法。"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:618 94e36c83287b492b9fc9a3a0f33e1c34
msgid ""
"Mission Planner displays Altitude of -21 million or NaN appearing in "
"Advanced Parameter list"
msgstr "Mission Planner 显示高度为 -2100 万或高级参数列表中出现 NaN"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:620 61779205857c49b2ad74d878eb5cb28c
msgid ""
"You should not attempt to fly your copter in this state because "
":ref:`AltHold <altholdmode>` will not function at all. You should instead go"
" into the Mission Planner's Terminal screen and reset your parameters by "
"typing \"setup\", \"reset\", \"Y\" and rebooting your APM."
msgstr ""
"在此状态下您不应尝试飞行您的 Copter，因为 :ref:`AltHold <altholdmode>` 将完全无法工作。您应进入 Mission "
"Planner 的终端屏幕并通过输入\"setup\"、\"reset\"、\"Y\"并重启 APM 来重置参数。"

#: ../../source/docs/troubleshooting.rst:626 2834e60c8673473680c9374f2a7fdcce
msgid ""
"The cause is a bug in the 2.9.1 accelerometer calibration routine that can "
"save NaN to the AHRS AHRS Trim parameters if the calibration routine fails. "
"This feeds into the inertial navigation routines and results in the bizarre "
"altitude display in the mission planner. Note: you will likely have seen "
"\"Calibration failed (????)\" after you attempted to calibrate the "
"accelerometers values."
msgstr ""
"原因是 2.9.1 版加速度计校准程序中的一个错误，该错误会在校准程序失败时将 NaN 保存到 AHRS 微调参数中。这会影响惯性导航程序，导致 "
"Mission Planner 中出现奇异的高度显示。注意：在尝试校准加速度计值后，您可能会看到\"Calibration failed "
"(????)\"的提示。"
